        {
          "left": "seedha",
          "right": "straight"
        },
        {
          "left": "ghar",
          "right": "home / house"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "These direction words are essential for navigating. 'Seedha' (straight), 'baayein' (left), and 'daayein' (right) are the three most important direction words."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s3-l9-ex02",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "question": "How do you ask 'Where is the market?' in Hindi?",
      "options": [
        "Bazaar kahaan hai?",
        "Kahaan bazaar hai?",
        "Bazaar hai kahaan?",
        "Kya bazaar hai?"
      ],
      "correctIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "'Bazaar kahaan hai?' — the subject comes first, then the question word 'kahaan' (where), then the verb 'hai' (is). This is the standard pattern for 'Where is ___?' questions."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s3-l9-ex03",
      "type": "translation",
      "prompt": "How do you say 'Go straight' in Hindi?",
      "direction": "from_english",
      "correct": "seedha jaaiye",
      "acceptedVariants": [
        "seedha jaao",
        "seedha jaiye"
      ],
      "explanation": "'Seedha jaaiye' is the polite way to say 'go straight'. 'Jaaiye' is the formal/polite form of the verb 'jaana' (to go). 'Seedha jaao' is the informal version.",
      "hint": "sounds like: seedha jaaiye"
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s3-l9-ex04",
      "type": "fill_in_blank",
      "sentence": "___ kahaan hai?",
      "correct": "school",
      "acceptedVariants": [
        "ghar",
        "bazaar"
      ],
      "explanation": "The pattern '___ kahaan hai?' means 'Where is ___?'. You can insert any place: 'school kahaan hai?' (Where is the school?), 'ghar kahaan hai?' (Where is the house?)."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s3-l9-ex05",
      "type": "word_ordering",
      "prompt": "Say: Turn left",
      "tiles": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "text": "muriye"
        },
        {
          "id": "t2",
          "text": "baayein"
        }
      ],
      "correctOrder": [
        "t2",
        "t1"
      ],
      "explanation": "'Baayein muriye' means 'Turn left' (polite). 'Baayein' (left) comes first, then 'muriye' (turn, polite form). For right, say 'daayein muriye'."
    },
    {
      "id": "hi-s3-l9-ex06",
